              "slots": {
                "main": {
                  "contentmodel": "wikitext",
                  "contentformat": "text/x-wiki",
                  "*": "=={{int:filedesc}}==\n{{Information\n|description={{en|1=Wadi Rum is a spectacularly scenic desert valley in southern Jordan. Masses of soaring cliffs and sandstone and granite mountains. Wadi Rum is Arabic for \"Roman Valley\", or \"Valley of the Rum\", as the Greeks (or East Romans) were called in the early Byzantine era by Arab people, probably referring to Christian Byzantine monastic or ascetic communities in the area. The area has been used as a background setting in a number of films (Red Planet, Prometheus, The Martian, Rogue One: A Star Wars Story, and many more).}}\n{{ru|1=Вади Рам (وادي رم‎), \"Лунная долина\" — пустыня в Иордании. Каменистая пустыня, песчаник и гранит, отдельные сухие деревья и кустарники, горы, каньоны, провалы и возвышенности.}}\n|date=2007-06-04 15:46:49\n|source={{own}}\n|author=[[User:Argenberg|Vyacheslav Argenberg]]\n|permission=© Vyacheslav Argenberg\n|other versions=\n}}\n\n{{User:Argenberg/Notes}}\n\n=={{int:license-header}}==\n{{User:Argenberg/License}}\n\n[[Category:Wadi Rum]]\n[[Category:Jordan]]\n[[Category:Photos by Vyacheslav Argenberg]]\n[[Category:Deserts of Jordan]]\n[[Category:Rock formations in Jordan]]\n[[Category:Plants in Wadi Rum]]\n[[Category:Photos by Vyacheslav Argenberg in Jordan]]\n[[Category:Photos by Vyacheslav Argenberg in 2007]]"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
